{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3db206e08ecd090e5882d84f1eeb41002c0fa7a85d6a7eca655d696c0e41a64e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14adda283cafe3157e641b0bb15a51ff361c0aabf3d0954a4051f44be90267c6","slc_86343d2d4629f00e9c73b7589adcc416ac093d39a70f3a1cc2f9a4fc1b3653c0"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"The project is alpha software whose APIs, schemas, and configuration may change between releases; adapter depth varies by runtime across OpenClaw, Claude Code, Codex, CrewAI, LangGraph, AutoGen, and Claude SDK workflows.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.5,"id":"clm_49dc6997e4999232c94d74715e6289759fe319031d3c8079472c66ca3b77e235","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=inference; facet=evaluation","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ae9e0fbbf253a006b65b741b938570aa85e80da395f9edf2508f8aa3b2ad13bf"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"The README's governance row lists 'evals' among shipped surfaces, suggesting the product includes evaluation features for agent work, though the snapshot does not describe how they score agent behavior.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7bf0ee6e9e9ccf49e3f5e75dd8ca065cd8945fb1241cf1982dc4901dacd630e4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5e502b7dc8d08377d1cdda3e36c7f4ee0c68d0e27055eaec4b57cd7e64d2a949"],"source_ids":["src_19113c342f5450e1bb011989a213d89b"],"text":"Host CLI dispatch gained opt-in sandbox flags: an allowlist-validated allowedTools, a clamped --max-budget-usd, and a workspace-scoped cwd escape-protected via MC_WORKSPACE_ROOT, sourced from agents.config with per-task overrides.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_881fd3310242eacce597cdc31baa3afa64859eeff23f9fbb4deede013d8d3894","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d7f0b16d7eeee31fcd33af6c77862a0fcca9a641683ea3f3b72b0bcec388d51"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"The control plane sits above agent runtimes and does not replace their reasoning or tool loops; it provides operators a single place to observe and govern work around those loops.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_92ca659ee377200f5bb9a48f82bbb9c689f4803738b6083b3b2d932dec2612d7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_39ee7bf728bf2adddd123f198b7615da25988f90eafdc08f87b32bf1c30bb35e"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"A gateway is optional for task, project, agent, scheduler, webhook, alert, and cost work, but live session messaging requires a connected runtime gateway; strict workspaces block deployment-level integrations until resources carry workspace ownership.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_acc01c493b6d65eca36cb81bbb7f8d144ffcf906033660352e97bbc14540946e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_60c5c5f99e088381ac7cad5732e211c8a1549857aca3adc29cb329ed38fa40f2","slc_6c1d35ede2fc28c62c6df0f25fed4c2f1d9a1a771076f7ff93e02a36bfdb4f4c","slc_70fbb61cb27b8f7fc52a2e1f6ff0634fbbc1c4006c50063f7a9a449501b8e17e","slc_8a9d2907f6fa49333cbd567e32a7d8058647c05c23a62d8280aaa2e6e1a41224"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"A gateway-free REST loop is documented: agents register via POST /api/agents/register, create work via POST /api/tasks, and claim queues via GET /api/tasks/queue?agent=..., authenticated with a Bearer API key.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e71168c87c92f1d92b7faf845eae5732443da0988d9706e72a13e3c8af1bc741","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9f1b038ba2a475bc449e9366cf3d2b0add397a0d5811ff4d2caf55f14598db73","slc_c501c3c90ac6de9910b10ad3741bffb2f22fd699a948fcc76c78af3498da73b7"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"Tasks flow through inbox, assignment, execution, review, quality review, and completion; Aegis review requires an approval record before a task reaches done, and recurring task templates create dated work on cron schedules.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f923958367d213c9a4ff609d64378513868906b7f6820503551601c0e855a714","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_38f552b41886fa6e34934837601b9dec9969bf4a1d3794e8847cdfb12e3ebe8d","slc_e06d88d780ca786268d34677efe6b3241dda24bdc93cca6130b7c8244cef02c8"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"Mission Control is described as a self-hosted control plane for operating AI agents: dispatching tasks, inspecting runs, reviewing failures, tracking spend, and coordinating runtimes from a local dashboard backed by SQLite.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_facf661e17006c4b425634c6ca1741d48ef902659e4a7c3cae341b855aa81e33","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36eb9734eba5477f8213c6920b01311f143d3718dfe024834fb2ded11a81be30","slc_ae9e0fbbf253a006b65b741b938570aa85e80da395f9edf2508f8aa3b2ad13bf"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"The product exposes a Web UI, CLI, MCP server, OpenAPI-described REST API, WebSocket, and SSE; a running instance serves interactive docs at /docs and OpenAPI JSON at /api/docs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fbd9518347539ed3c5697cd16b12588bd40d3cd01b1aa5cc9cee0ff966be8512","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"builderz-labs/mission-control@5483a0e1eef1 snapshot 8467a0c3e4579618","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ae9e0fbbf253a006b65b741b938570aa85e80da395f9edf2508f8aa3b2ad13bf"],"source_ids":["src_c2986d600f5f5b2c8e00b90b7dbea97b"],"text":"Shipped surfaces include task inbox/assignment/review with an Aegis quality gate and completion receipts, agent registration and sessions, activity/schedules/alerts/webhooks/cost views, memory browser and skills registry, and governance features like roles, API keys, approvals, audits, and evals.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:59:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ac06344d7cff4aa680da1718b645c17d"}
